---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import volt_logo from '../../assets/voltstein_logo.png';
import volt_1 from '../../assets/voltstein_1.png';
import volt_2 from '../../assets/voltstein_2.jpg';
---

<Layout
	title="Portfolio - Voltstein (2009)"
	description="Portfolio - Voltstein"
	pubDate={new Date('September 8 2026')}
	/*heroImage="/blog-placeholder-about.jpg"*/
>
	<p>
		Professor von Voltstein's Capacitor Conundrum was an unreleased game from 2009 by Puny Human wherein 
		you play as a mad scientist solving puzzles in order to bring monsters to life.
	</p>
	<center>
		<Image src={volt_logo} width=500 alt="Professor von Voltstein's Capacitor Conundrum main menu" />
	</center>

	<p>
		Puzzles consisted of various electrical components that would modify the "sparks" that ran along 
		the wire (which the player would place). Some example puzzle pieces that could appear on the board:
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li><b>Resistor:</b> Decreases the voltage of a spark that passes through it by 1.</li>
		<li><b>Amplifier:</b> Increases the voltage of a spark that passes through it by 1.</li>
		<li><b>Transformer:</b> Changes the color of a spark that passes through it.</li>
		<li><b>Capacitor:</b> Repeatedly outputs a copy of the spark that entered it based on the number on the capacitor.</li>
	</ul>

	<br/>

	<center>
		<Image src={volt_1} alt="a Professor von Voltstein's Capacitor Conundrum puzzle" />
		<i>An example puzzle with various components.</i>
	</center>

	<p>
		The game consisted of various modes, including the classic puzzle mode where you just have to solve 
		a single puzzle, bringing one monster to life. In addition, there was a survival mode, where the player 
		would have to solve numerous puzzles in a row with randomized layouts. Each puzzle solved would spawn 
		a monster to fight off villagers attacking the castle, represented in a horizontal bar at the top 
		of the screen.
	</p>

	<center>
		<Image src={volt_2} alt="a Professor von Voltstein's Capacitor Conundrum puzzle" />
		<i>Another example puzzle with different assets.</i>
	</center>
	</p>
</Layout>
